=== Parity with web source (data / composition / states / i18n) ===
  data sources: useVehicleSettings (resolver effective-setting feed), useUpsertVehicleSetting (PUT),
                useResetVehicleSetting (DELETE) → all bound via the VehicleSettingsSource P1/S8 seam
                (no HTTP in the view).
  composition : GlassPanel header 'Per-vehicle settings' + subtitle; one row per supported key in the
                web order (nickname/mute_until/charge_cost_tariff_id/units_distance/units_temperature/
                units_energy) with label + help, the typed input (text field / unit picker /
                date-and-time control), the source pill (Override|User default|Vehicle name|System
                default), a Save button (enabled only when the draft is dirty & not saving) and a
                Reset-to-default button (enabled only for override rows & not resetting). mute_until is
                edited as a Date and persisted as RFC3339 (web datetime-local ⇄ RFC3339).
  states      : loading (3 skeleton rows) / empty (defensive friendly state) / error (+retry) / data;
                + connection axis (live/stale/offline chip + banner, one-shot stale auto-refresh);
                + per-row inline validation (required / invalid / invalid-date) and save/reset
                in-flight + failure states. Every state has a #Preview.
  i18n        : table "VehicleSettingsTab"; every web 'vehicleSettings.*' key preserved verbatim
                (title/subtitle/loading/error/source.*/actions.*/keys.*.{label,help}/validation.*/
                toasts.*/errors.*) + native chrome keys; no English literals in Swift
                (facade NSLocalizedString(key, value: fallback)).
  a11y        : VoiceOver labels on every interactive control (inputs, Save/Reset, refresh, clear/set);
                row header composed as "{label}, {source}" with .isHeader; source-pill label exposed;
                Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce Motion via TSFadeIn/TSSkeleton.
  telemetry   : VehicleSettingsTabModel.start() emits the P1/S11 'view.opened' event
                surface='VehicleSettingsTab' once (asserted in tests).

